<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms seek 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms seek 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd jointly invited tenders to buy a total of 21,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat, traders said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Of the total, Cheiljedang has invited tenders for 12,000 tonnes at basis over May futures on the U.S grain futures exchanges including the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour has invited the remaining 9,500 tonnes at flat prices.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for May 5-June 5 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
